---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Doc from '../components/legal/Doc.astro';
const updated = '30 October 2026';
// Shows a draft note and keeps the page out of search until the placeholders are filled (design/legal/README.md).
const draft = true;
---

<Base title="Terms of use · Comarket" description="The rules for using comarket.si and the waitlist, and the general terms behind the Brand and Creator agreements." stage="none" noindex={draft}>
  <Doc
    title="Terms of use"
    lede="The rules for this site and the waitlist. The general terms at the end also apply to the Brand and Creator agreements."
    updated={updated}
    draft={draft}
    current="/terms"
  >
    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">1.1</span>These terms are between you and [[LEGAL ENTITY NAME]], a [[STATE OF FORMATION]] company at
      [[REGISTERED ADDRESS]] ("Comarket", "we", "us"). Contact: <a href="mailto:[[CONTACT EMAIL]]">[[CONTACT EMAIL]]</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">1.2</span>By using comarket.si or joining the waitlist, you accept these terms and our
      <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>. If you act for a company, you accept for it and confirm you may.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Using the site</h2>
    <p><span class="n">2.1</span>Don't:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>use bots or scripts to sign up, check handles, request previews or copy the site;</li>
      <li>sign up with someone else's email, or claim a handle or brand you have no right to;</li>
      <li>try to break or get around the site's security, rate limits or bot check (report security issues to [[CONTACT EMAIL]]); or</li>
      <li>use the site to break the law.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. The waitlist</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.1</span>You must be 18 or older and joining for a business or your own creator work.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.2</span>Joining holds your place. It isn't an order, and neither of us has to sign anything further. We
      decide when and in what order places open. Your pass number has no cash value and can't be transferred.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.3</span>A creator handle you claim (comarket.si/yourname) is kept for you while you're on the waitlist and
      while your creator account is open. It's a right to use an address, not property. We may withdraw a handle that
      impersonates someone, uses a name or trademark you have no right to, or is offensive, and we'll offer you another.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.4</span>We record the fee rates shown to a brand when it joins. If our rates are higher when you sign the
      Brand Agreement, we apply the rates you were shown for your first 12 months.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.5</span>You may share your referral link. Don't spam it or create entries for people who didn't ask. No
      reward for referrals is promised.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.6</span>We email you a confirmation and once more when your spot opens. You can leave at any time by
      emailing [[CONTACT EMAIL]].
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.7</span>When you type a website, our server reads its public homepage to build a preview. Previews are
      mock-ups and aren't published.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Examples on the site</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">4.1</span>The brands, creators, posts, sales and earnings shown on the site are fictional examples. They
      aren't testimonials, typical results or promises. Where a summary on the site differs from the Brand or Creator
      Agreement, the agreement applies.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Our rights</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">5.1</span>We own the site, its design, code and content, and the Comarket name. You may use the site as these
      terms allow, and nothing more. If you send us feedback, we may use it freely.
    </p>

    <h2>6. No warranty and limited liability</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">6.1</span>The site and the waitlist are free and provided "as is", without warranties of any kind, to the
      extent the law allows.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">6.2</span>We aren't liable for lost profits or indirect, incidental or consequential damages. Our total
      liability for the site and the waitlist is limited to $100.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">6.3</span>We may change or stop the site or the waitlist, or remove an entry that breaks these terms, at any
      time.
    </p>

    <h2>7. General terms</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">7.1</span>This section also applies to the <a href="/brand-terms">Brand Agreement</a> and the
      <a href="/creator-terms">Creator Agreement</a> (each an "Agreement"). If it conflicts with an Agreement, the Agreement
      applies.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">7.2</span><b>Accounts.</b> Keep your login safe and your details accurate. You're responsible for activity on
      your account. One account per person or business.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">7.3</span><b>Changes.</b> We may change these terms or an Agreement. We'll email you at least 15 days before a
      change takes effect (30 days for a change to fees). If you don't accept it, you may end the Agreement before then; fees
      and earnings on sales already made stay payable. We may act sooner where the law requires, or to stop fraud or a
      security threat.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">7.4</span><b>Confidentiality.</b> Each side keeps the other's non-public business information confidential,
      uses it only for the Agreement, and may disclose it only where the law requires. This lasts for the Agreement and two
      years after.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">7.5</span><b>Notices.</b> We send notices to your account email. You send them to [[CONTACT EMAIL]].
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">7.6</span><b>Disputes.</b> Before going to court, write to us and we'll both try for 30 days to settle it.
      These terms and each Agreement are governed by the laws of [[STATE OF FORMATION]] and applicable US federal law. Any
      lawsuit must be brought in the state or federal courts located in [[STATE OF FORMATION]], and both sides consent to their
      jurisdiction. Either side may instead use small claims court where the claim qualifies.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">7.7</span><b>Everything else.</b> Neither side is liable for delays caused by events outside its reasonable
      control, though this doesn't excuse paying money owed. You may not transfer an Agreement without our consent; we may
      transfer it to a buyer of our business. The parties are independent contractors, except for the limited payment
      collection role in the Brand and Creator agreements. Each Agreement, with the documents it refers to, is the whole
      agreement on its subject. If part is unenforceable, the rest still applies. Not enforcing a right doesn't waive it. You
      confirm you are not on a US sanctions list.
    </p>
  </Doc>
  <Footer />
</Base>
